"""Mnemosyne site server for ai-memory.net.

Serves the account API and the GitHub OAuth callback. Standard library only.

Why the accounts are ours: WorkBuddy's hosted auth is bound to the domain it
was registered on and calls `/.cloud/auth/**` relatively — on ai-memory.net
those requests have nowhere to go (404), which is exactly what "network
unavailable" was. So accounts live here: PBKDF2-hashed passwords, sessions in
a cookie, no third-party dependency.

Layout — the two roots are deliberately different:
  APP_ROOT  /opt/mnemosyne-site    server.py, oauth.config.json, users/sessions
  WEB_ROOT  /var/www/ai-memory     index.html, assets/   ← served by Caddy
Keeping the secrets OUT of WEB_ROOT is what stops them being downloadable.
"""

